{
	"metadata": {
		"name": "ELSA-d Thruster Failures",
		"description": "A studio docking-reference demonstration inspired by ELSA-d. The Servicer starts about 10 m along-track from the Client, with the Client attitude rotated so its docking adapter initially faces the Servicer. Dock pointing maintains the mirrored docking-adapter Up axes (with clocking), then a port-relative rendezvous flies a 5 m standoff along the Client port axis and a slower alignment-gated closure to capture. Thruster-fault events are included but disabled so this run completes a clean dock as a baseline."
